root = Quiz("Essential PixiJS Vocabulary Quiz", [qVoc1, qVoc2])

qVoc1 = QuizQuestion(
  "q_voc_1",
  "What is the structural difference between a 'Texture' and a 'BaseTexture' in PixiJS?",
  [
    QuizChoice(
      "c1",
      "Texture is for 3D meshes; BaseTexture is for 2D sprites",
      false,
      "PixiJS is a 2D rendering engine; both handle 2D image data.",
    ),
    QuizChoice(
      "c2",
      "BaseTexture holds the actual raw WebGL GPU image resource, while Texture defines a specific UV rectangular crop of that BaseTexture",
      true,
      "BaseTexture owns the GPU memory allocation. Multiple Texture instances can reference sub-regions (UV frames) of the same BaseTexture, enabling sprite sheets.",
    ),
    QuizChoice(
      "c3",
      "BaseTexture is rendered by CPU, whereas Texture is rendered by GPU",
      false,
      "Both are part of the GPU texture management system.",
    ),
    QuizChoice(
      "c4",
      "They are identical aliases with no technical distinction",
      false,
      "They have distinct responsibilities: GPU resource vs UV sub-region definition.",
    ),
  ],
  "Think about how a sprite sheet texture atlas shares one large image across dozens of sprite frames.",
)

qVoc2 = QuizQuestion(
  "q_voc_2",
  "How does the 'Ticker' deltaTime property help maintain consistent movement speed across different monitor refresh rates (60Hz vs 144Hz)?",
  [
    QuizChoice(
      "c1",
      "It forces all monitors to run at exactly 60 FPS by sleeping the thread",
      false,
      "Ticker does not sleep the main JS thread; it measures actual elapsed time.",
    ),
    QuizChoice(
      "c2",
      "It provides a frame duration multiplier proportional to 60 FPS, scaling velocity so distance per second remains identical",
      true,
      "At 60 FPS, deltaTime is ~1.0. At 120 FPS, deltaTime is ~0.5. Multiplying velocity by deltaTime ensures identical movement speed in physical time.",
    ),
    QuizChoice(
      "c3",
      "It skips rendering every second frame on high-refresh monitors",
      false,
      "PixiJS renders on every RAF frame to deliver maximum visual smoothness.",
    ),
    QuizChoice(
      "c4",
      "It converts pixel measurements to meters automatically",
      false,
      "Pixel measurements are preserved; deltaTime scales numerical step changes.",
    ),
  ],
  "Consider what multiplier is needed when a frame executes in 8.3ms (120Hz) instead of 16.6ms (60Hz).",
)
